    { m: "M4", issue: 5, title: "UWP support", state: "now", pct: 60, note: "Cuphead is advancing through the native runtime walls one by one under the mrt100/ntdll harness. CLEARED: ntdll WNF abort, profapi.114 AppContainer-storage abort, MrmCoreR RtlReportException livelock, package activation (status 0, mrt100 native, GetCurrentPackageInfo3 + StateRepository cache resolve), the Windows.UI.Core.CoreWindow activation factory (builtin windows.ui corewindow.c), winemac.drv GUI-session window creation (real 1280×720 CoreWindow), SHCORE.265 GetScaleFactorForCoreWindow (S_OK default-scale EXPERIMENT fallback), the bcp47mrm.dll 12-function delay-import wall (new builtin Wine dll, honest semi-stubs), AND — new in run6 — the Windows.ApplicationModel.Core.CoreApplication activation-factory wall (hr 0x80040111). That one was root-caused and fixed: the CrossOver wine wrapper STRIPS the WINEDLLOVERRIDES env var, so the harness's env-based twinapi.appcore=n was silently dropped and Wine loaded its builtin twinapi.appcore (no CoreApplication factory). Passing the override via wine argv (--dll twinapi.appcore=n) loads twinapi.appcore ': native', resolves the factory, and lets activation succeed (status 0) — the app now runs 11s and creates its real 1280×720 window. CURRENT FRONTIER: the CoreWindow is created lazily (EXPERIMENT GetForCurrentThread path, not a genuine IFrameworkView::SetWindow host) and is never Activated/shown (visible=0), so the app exits 92 before any D3D12/swapchain init; and the app's QI for the classic ICoreWindow IID {9ac40241-…} hits E_NOINTERFACE (tolerated). Next: answer the classic ICoreWindow IID + drive genuine view-host/Activate so the HWND shows and the render loop reaches CreateSwapChainForCoreWindow. windows.ui/combase hosting lane, shared with Celeste. Bottle teardown verified clean. run7/run8 (Oct 11) tested — and DISPROVED — the theory that combase's unimplemented CoGetSystemSecurityPermissions caused exit 92: run7 deployed Celeste's newer combase (52ed4c9a) into bottle system32 with NO effect (Wine loads the builtin combase from the shared wine tree, not system32); run8 deployed it into the shared-tree builtin path and DID remove the abort, but the app then REGRESSED — it fast-fails (0xC0000409) at 944ms with 0 windows immediately after QI'ing a real ICoreWindow IID (7a5b6fd1) that Wine's CoreWindow cannot provide. So run6/7 actually TOLERATED the abort and got further (windows created); the 52ed4c9a build drift is unsuitable for Cuphead, and the swap was reverted to the a6d35827 baseline. Confirmed root cause: Wine's CoreWindow never exposes the ICoreWindow interface the app needs (9ac40241 old-path / 7a5b6fd1 new-path), so the window is never driven/shown — the faithful fix is a windows.ui corewindow.c ICoreWindow-IID + genuine view-host patch (needs a build + SDK-provenance check + Celeste coordination)." },
    { m: "M5", issue: 6, title: "EAppx support", state: "blocked", pct: 25, note: "EAppxBundle titles not installable/playable. Package identity/activation seams progressing in the side session." },
    { m: "M3", issue: 4, title: "Engine detect / switch / default / per-game", state: "now", pct: 60, note: "PR #13: pure EngineRouting.decide (package type x per-game override x default x availability) consumed by the launch path; a selected engine that isn't installed refuses launch and is never substituted (verified). Adversarial REVISE fix verified correct: the availability detector now probes each provider's own registered runner path, so a per-game override to any installed engine is detected instead of being falsely refused. Rebase onto merged-M10 foundation pending before merge. (Oct 11)" },
    { m: "M10", issue: 11, title: "Account tiers (free / subscription)", state: "done", pct: 85, note: "Two-axis AccountEntitlements (free/Game Pass plan/owned) with pure derive(); eligibility classifier where install alone yields only installedUnknown, never Owned. PR #12 MERGED into foundation (b8dbc62). Self-adversarial hardening confirmed in trunk: model moved to XodusManagement with real Tests/ManagementChecks fixtures; stale/unloaded/busy evidence no longer establishes tiers; the identity-less global probe is kept separate from tier derivation. Perks/leaving-soon deferred (no real source). (Oct 11)" }
